/**
 * @defgroup IdsmGeo IdsmGeo — Inner Detector Support Module Geometry
 * @ingroup StarVMCGeometry
 * @brief AGML geometry for the STAR Inner Detector Support Module (IDSM).
 *
 * @details
 * The Inner Detector Support Module (IDSM) is the mechanical backbone and TGeo mother
 * volume for STAR's Heavy Flavour Tracker (HFT) system. It is a large cylindrical support
 * structure fabricated primarily from carbon-fibre reinforced polymer (CFRP) and aluminium,
 * enclosing the three HFT sub-detectors — the Pixel Detector (PXL, r ≈ 2.8 and 8 cm), the
 * Intermediate Silicon Tracker (IST, r ≈ 14 cm), and the Silicon Strip Detector (SSD,
 * r ≈ 23 cm) — within a single coherent mechanical frame. In geometry versions 1 and 2 it
 * also provides mount points for FGT (Forward GEM Tracker) cable rails and disk cables.
 *
 * The AGML detector tag is @c IDSM. The control structure @c IDSC holds the geometry
 * @c version number. Detailed structural parameters are in @c IDSG (radii, FGT layout,
 * TPC resistor tube geometry) and alignment parameters in @c IDSA (Euler angles for
 * placement in the cave frame, defaulting to identity).
 *
 * The IDSM mother volume @c IDSM is a @c TUBE (or zero-inner-radius envelope in v2+)
 * placed in the cave with the rotation defined by @c IDSA. All HFT sub-detector volumes
 * (PXMO, IBMO, SFMO) are placed as daughters inside @c IDSM by the geometry steering.
 *
 * @par Main structural elements
 * - @c SUCA — central CF tube, r = 21.5–21.6 cm, dz = 56 cm
 * - @c SUCB — small Al ring at central tube, r = 21.6–22.4 cm
 * - @c SUCC — CF cone section connecting central tube to outer cylinders
 * - @c SUCD — large Al ring at cone junction, r = 38.6–39.9 cm
 * - @c SUCE — east/west CF outer cylinder, r = 39.8–39.9 cm, dz = 80.8 cm
 * - @c SUCF — large Al ring at outer cylinder end, r = 40.0–40.5 cm
 * - @c SUCG — large Al end disk, r = 10.3–40.5 cm
 * - @c TPRR / @c TPRT — TPC resistor tubes and FR4 protection at r ≈ 43 cm
 * - @c FGRL / @c FGHV — FGT rails and cable bundles (versions 1 and 2 only)
 *
 * @par AGML module files
 * - IdsmGeo1.xml  — @c IDSMGEO1  (Apr 2011, Balewski/Leight; 2012 beam support cone,
 *                    geometry versions 1.0 and 2.0; includes FGT rails/cables)
 * - IdsmGeo2.xml  — @c IDSMGEO2  (Apr 2011/updated, Balewski/Leight/Videbaek; 2013 cone
 *                    with ewcs parameters; inner radius = 0 in v2+; v14 strips FGT cables)
 * - IdsmGeo2a.xml — @c IDSMGEO2A (as IdsmGeo2 with alignment rotation from @c IDSA;
 *                    v14 = y2014 production geometry without FGT cables)
 *
 * @par Configuration setups (IdsmConfig.xml)
 * - @c IDSMof   — IDSM disabled
 * - @c IDSMon / @c IDSM01 — IdsmGeo1, version=1 (Run 12, 2012)
 * - @c IDSM02   — IdsmGeo2, version=2 (Run 13, 2013)
 * - @c IDSM14   — IdsmGeo2, version=14 (y2014, no FGT cables)
 * - @c IDSM02a  — IdsmGeo2a, version=2 (Run 13 with alignment)
 * - @c IDSM14a  — IdsmGeo2a, version=14 (y2014 production, no FGT cables)
 *
 * @{
 */

/**
 * @defgroup IdsmGeoV1 IdsmGeo1 (IDSMGEO1) — 2012 beam support cone
 * @ingroup IdsmGeo
 * @brief Simplified IDSM geometry for Run 12 (J. Balewski / W. Leight, Apr 2011).
 * @details Initial IDSM geometry defining the six primary structural volumes:
 * central CF tube (SUCA), small Al ring (SUCB), CF cone (SUCC), large Al ring (SUCD),
 * east/west CF cylinder (SUCE), and Al end ring (SUCF). Also includes the end Al disk
 * (SUCG), TPC resistor tubes (TPRR/TPRT), FGT rails (FGRL, TUBE r = 0.9–1.0 cm,
 * dz = 82.8 cm), and FGT cable bundles (FGHV, TUBE r = 0–0.43 cm) for 6 disk positions.
 * The @c IDSG structure carries two fill versions: 1.0 (2012 geometry) and 2.0 (2013
 * update with different FGT cable positions). Inner radius @c rF = 2.25 cm in both.
 * Activated by @c IDSMon and @c IDSM01.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup IdsmGeoV2 IdsmGeo2 (IDSMGEO2) — 2013 beam support cone
 * @ingroup IdsmGeo
 * @brief Updated IDSM geometry for Run 13+ (Balewski/Leight/Videbaek, updated 2013).
 * @details Extends IdsmGeo1 by introducing @c IDSG.ewcsInnerRad and @c IDSG.ewcsOuterRad
 * parameters for the east/west cone section. In geometry version 2 the inner radius is
 * set to 0 (allowing the beam pipe to be placed inside IDSM as a daughter). Geometry
 * version 14 (y2014) removes the FGT cable volumes to reflect the actual y2014 detector
 * configuration. Activated by @c IDSM02 (v2) and @c IDSM14 (v14).
 */

/**
 * @defgroup IdsmGeoV2a IdsmGeo2a (IDSMGEO2A) — 2013/y2014 geometry with alignment
 * @ingroup IdsmGeo
 * @brief IDSM geometry with @c IDSA alignment rotation (Balewski/Leight/Videbaek).
 * @details Structurally identical to IdsmGeo2, but applies the full rotation matrix from
 * the @c IDSA structure when placing @c IDSM in the cave. The default ideal alignment
 * corresponds to identity (thetax=90°, phix=0°, thetay=90°, phiy=90°, thetaz=0°,
 * phiz=0°). Non-trivial values of these angles encode a physical misalignment of the
 * IDSM as built. Version 14 is the default y2014 production geometry (no FGT cables).
 * Activated by @c IDSM02a (v2) and @c IDSM14a (v14, production).
 */

/**
 * @}
 */
